<title>CROATIA: Croatian Rijecka Banka reverts to profit in 1996.</title>
<headline>Croatian Rijecka Banka reverts to profit in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>ZAGREB 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results for calendar 1996.</p>
<p>(Millions of kuna unless otherwise stated.)</p>
<p>					   1996	  1995</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		     2.4	(890.5)</p>
<p>    Net profit			 n.a.	  n.a.</p>
<p>    Interest income		 235.2	 228.7</p>
<p>    Interest costs		 (158.9)     (137.8)</p>
<p>    Net adjustments		  (3.3)     (567.2)</p>
<p>    Operating result		 (2.4)     (889.6)</p>
<p>    Extraordinary profit	    4.8	  (0.9)</p>
<p>    Dividend (kuna per share)    n.a.	  none</p>
<p>    Assets (bln kuna)		 4.1	   3.8</p>
<p>NOTES - The bank has been overhauled and recapitalised under a government programme, which began in 1996. -- Zagreb Newsroom, 385 1 4557075</p>
